Materialize GPTQ embed gathers as row-major activations.

INCLinearMethod.embedding (patches/inc-gptq-embed.patch) unpacks GPTQ columns
into w of shape [H, T] and returns w.t(). That transpose is a view:
stride(1)==T, not 1. Marlin then dies on the first GDN in_proj_qkvz with
"A.stride(1) is not 1" — including under --enforce-eager, because this is
not an Inductor bug. One .contiguous() at gather time; residual/RMSNorm
empty_like then stay row-major so later GEMMs do not copy.

Apply after inc-gptq-embed.patch:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/inc-gptq-z-embed-contiguous.patch

Validated against vLLM 0.28.0.

--- a/model_executor/layers/quantization/inc/inc_linear.py
+++ b/model_executor/layers/quantization/inc/inc_linear.py
@@ -62,4 +62,7 @@
             (qw.unsqueeze(1) >> shifts.view(1, pack, 1)) & maxq
         ).reshape(-1, ids.numel()).float() - zp
         w = (q * sc.repeat_interleave(group, dim=0)).to(layer.scales.dtype)
-        return w.t().reshape(*x.shape, -1)
+        # w is [H, T] (GPTQ columns). .t() is a view with stride(1)=T;
+        # Marlin requires A.stride(1)==1 (marlin.cu:653). Materialize
+        # row-major [T, H] here — one copy per embed, not per GEMM.
+        return w.t().contiguous().reshape(*x.shape, -1)
